<% content_for(:title, "Privacy Policy - DataKeep") %>

<%= render "shared/landing_nav" %>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl pt-24 pb-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 bg-white dark:border-gray-800 dark:bg-white/[0.03]">
    <div class="px-6 py-8 sm:px-10 sm:py-10">

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">Last updated: March 15, 2026</p>

      <div class="mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">

        <%# ── 1. Introduction ────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">1. Introduction</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            DataKeep ("we," "us," or "our") operates the DataKeep database backup automation platform ("Service"). This Privacy Policy describes how we collect, use, store, and protect information when you use our Service.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We are an <strong>automation facilitator</strong> &mdash; we help you automate database backups, syncs, and restores. We process your data only as necessary to perform the operations you configure, and we do not access, inspect, or monetize your database content.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 2. Information We Collect ──────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">2. Information We Collect</h2>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.1 Account Information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">When you create an account, we collect:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
            <li>Full name</li>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Password (hashed with bcrypt; we never store plaintext passwords)</li>
            <li>OAuth provider ID (if you sign in with Google)</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.2 Database Connection Credentials</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            To perform backups, syncs, and restores, you provide database connection details including host, port, database name, username, and password. Database passwords are encrypted at rest using <strong>Active Record Encryption</strong> (AES-256-GCM) and are never stored in plaintext.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.3 Backup Data (Transient Processing)</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            During backup and restore operations, your database content passes through our infrastructure. This data is:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1 pl-6">
            <li>Held in temporary files only for the duration of the operation;</li>
            <li>Encrypted with AES-256-GCM if you enable the encryption option;</li>
            <li>Uploaded to your configured storage backend(s) and then deleted from our systems;</li>
            <li><strong>Never read, analyzed, indexed, or used for any purpose</strong> other than completing the requested operation.</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.4 Configuration and Operational Data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">We store information about your backup jobs, sync jobs, schedules, storage backend configurations, notification channel settings, and audit logs. This is necessary to operate the Service.</p>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.5 Billing Information</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            Payment processing is handled entirely by <strong>Stripe</strong>. We store your Stripe customer ID for reference but do not store credit card numbers, bank account details, or other sensitive payment data on our servers.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-medium text-gray-800 dark:text-gray-200">2.6 Usage and Log Data</h3>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We collect server logs, IP addresses, browser information, and audit trails for security monitoring, debugging, and abuse prevention.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 3. How We Use Your Information ─────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We use collected information exclusively to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li>Provide, operate, and maintain the Service;</li>
            <li>Execute backup, sync, and restore operations as you configure;</li>
            <li>Send transactional notifications (backup success/failure, account alerts);</li>
            <li>Process billing through Stripe;</li>
            <li>Monitor system health and prevent abuse;</li>
            <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="mt-3 rounded-lg border border-green-200 bg-green-50 p-4 dark:border-green-800/50 dark:bg-green-900/20">
            <p class="font-medium text-green-800 dark:text-green-200">
              We do NOT: sell your data, use it for advertising, share it with third-party data brokers, train machine learning models on it, or profile you for marketing purposes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <%# ── 4. Data Storage & Encryption ───────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">4. Data Storage and Encryption</h2>
          <table class="mt-3 w-full text-left text-sm">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
                <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Data Type</th>
                <th class="py-2 font-medium text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Encryption</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-800">
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Database passwords</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (Active Record Encryption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">VPN configuration data</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (Active Record Encryption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Backup encryption keys</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (Active Record Encryption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Storage backend credentials</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (Active Record Encryption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Notification channel configs</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (Active Record Encryption)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">Backup files (when enabled)</td>
                <td class="py-2">AES-256-GCM (per-job unique key)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-2 pr-4">User passwords</td>
                <td class="py-2">bcrypt (one-way hash)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </section>

        <%# ── 5. Data Sharing ────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">5. Data Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">We share data only with:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> &mdash; for payment processing (subject to <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" class="text-primary-500 hover:text-primary-600 dark:hover:text-primary-400 underline" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stripe's Privacy Policy</a>);</li>
            <li><strong>Cloud infrastructure providers</strong> &mdash; our hosting infrastructure processes your data as part of normal operations;</li>
            <li><strong>Your configured storage backends</strong> &mdash; backup files are uploaded to destinations you specify;</li>
            <li><strong>Your configured notification channels</strong> &mdash; operational alerts are sent to Slack, Discord, Telegram, email, or webhook endpoints you configure;</li>
            <li><strong>Law enforcement</strong> &mdash; only when required by valid legal process (subpoena, court order, or equivalent).</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            We do not sell, rent, or lease your personal information or database content to any third party.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 6. Data Retention ──────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">6. Data Retention</h2>
          <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Account data:</strong> Retained while your account is active. Deleted within thirty (30) days of account termination.</li>
            <li><strong>Backup files on managed storage:</strong> Retained according to your configured retention policy. Deleted within thirty (30) days after account termination.</li>
            <li><strong>Backup files on your storage:</strong> Not under our control. You are responsible for their lifecycle.</li>
            <li><strong>Audit logs:</strong> Retained for twelve (12) months for security and compliance purposes.</li>
            <li><strong>Transient backup data:</strong> Deleted immediately after each operation completes.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <%# ── 7. Your Rights ─────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">7. Your Rights</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you;</li>
            <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate personal data;</li>
            <li><strong>Delete</strong> your account and associated data;</li>
            <li><strong>Export</strong> your configuration data;</li>
            <li><strong>Object to</strong> or restrict certain processing;</li>
            <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> where processing is based on consent.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            To exercise these rights, contact us at
            <a href="mailto:privacy@datakeep.io" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:text-primary-600 dark:hover:text-primary-400 underline">privacy@datakeep.io</a>.
            We will respond within thirty (30) days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 8. Cookies ─────────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">8. Cookies and Session Data</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We use essential session cookies to maintain your authenticated state. We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or third-party analytics that profile individual users. Cloudflare may set security cookies as part of our DDoS protection and CDN services.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 9. Security ────────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">9. Security Measures</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We implement industry-standard security measures including:
          </p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-6">
            <li>Encryption of sensitive data at rest (AES-256-GCM);</li>
            <li>Encryption of data in transit (TLS 1.2+);</li>
            <li>Password hashing with bcrypt;</li>
            <li>CSRF protection on all forms;</li>
            <li>Content Security Policy headers;</li>
            <li>Audit logging of security-relevant actions;</li>
            <li>Principle of least privilege for database connections.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-2">
            However, no system is 100% secure. You are responsible for securing your own credentials, storage backends, and database infrastructure.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 10. International Transfers ────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">10. International Data Transfers</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            Your data may be processed in jurisdictions where our infrastructure is hosted. By using the Service, you consent to the transfer of your information to these locations. We take appropriate safeguards to ensure your data remains protected in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 11. Children ───────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">11. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            The Service is not intended for use by individuals under the age of 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us with personal data, please contact us and we will delete it promptly.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── 12. Changes ────────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section>
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p class="mt-3">
            We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Material changes will be communicated via email or an in-app notice at least thirty (30) days before they take effect. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
          </p>
        </section>

        <%# ── Contact ────────────────────────────────────────── %>
        <section class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-5 dark:border-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-800/50">
          <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Contact</h2>
          <p class="mt-2">
            For privacy-related inquiries, contact our Data Protection Officer at
            <a href="mailto:privacy@datakeep.io" class="font-medium text-primary-500 hover:text-primary-600 dark:hover:text-primary-400 underline">privacy@datakeep.io</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <%# Navigation links %>
  <div class="mt-6 flex items-center justify-between text-sm text-gray-500 dark:text-gray-400">
    <%= link_to "&larr; Back".html_safe, :back, class: "hover:text-gray-700 dark:hover:text-gray-300" %>
    <%= link_to "&larr; Terms of Service".html_safe, terms_path, class: "hover:text-gray-700 dark:hover:text-gray-300" %>
  </div>
</div>
